Description: pvr: raise buffer descriptor limits, load only used descriptors
 The per-pipeline-layout limits are n times the Vulkan 1.0 per-stage minimum
 for the three supported stages. maxPerStageDescriptorStorageBuffers was
 later raised to 16 (8ee23ece2bd), but maxDescriptorSetStorageBuffers stayed
 at 3 * 4 = 12, below the per-stage value. wgpu reports
 min(maxPerStageDescriptorStorageBuffers, maxDescriptorSetStorageBuffers / 2)
 storage buffers per shader stage, which gives 6, and programs that need 10
 fail.
 .
 Use 3 * 16 storage buffers per pipeline layout. Raise
 maxPerStageDescriptorUniformBuffers from 13 to 15, the Vulkan 1.4 minimum,
 with 3 * 15 per pipeline layout. Report 8 dynamic storage buffers
 (PVR_MAX_DESCRIPTOR_SET_STORAGE_DYNAMIC_BUFFERS), the total that
 VK_KHR_maintenance7 already reports. Compute maxPerStageResources as the
 sum of the per-stage limits and maxColorAttachments, the value the
 specification requires when the sum is below 128.
 .
 Nothing in the driver is sized by these limits: a set layout is as large as
 its bindings (pvr_CreateDescriptorSetLayout()) and dynamic buffers live in
 the set (struct pvr_descriptor_set). The PDS descriptor program of a stage
 copies the descriptors into shared registers (pvr_setup_descriptors(),
 pvr_pds_descriptor_program_create_and_upload()), 1024 of them for a vertex
 or fragment task (ROGUE_MAX_VERTEX_SHARED_REGISTERS,
 ROGUE_MAX_PIXEL_SHARED_REGISTERS). A buffer descriptor is 4 dwords. A set
 layout holds the bindings of all stages, and a single set at the per-set
 limits is more than 1400 dwords (48 samplers of 12 dwords, 48 sampled
 images and 12 storage images of 8 dwords, 45 uniform and 48 storage buffers
 of 4 dwords), while several sets can be bound.
 .
 The PDS program therefore copies, for each used set, only the span from the
 first to the last binding the shader uses instead of the whole set. The
 binding ranges are relative to that span, and the PDS program gets the
 offset of the span in the set through the offset_in_dwords field of the
 descriptor set entry, which the command buffer adds to the address of the
 set. The start of the span is rounded down to a multiple of four dwords.
 Bindings the shader does not use get no range. Dynamic buffers are still
 copied for the whole set. If a stage still needs more shared registers than
 the hardware provides, pipeline creation fails with
 VK_ERROR_OUT_OF_DEVICE_MEMORY instead of overflowing the register file. The
 size of the shared registers that is stored in the render job was a uint8_t
 that cut every value above 255; it is now a uint32_t like the value it is
 copied from.
 .
 Only for this downstream stack; not intended for upstream submission.
